salami: enable cellular data path

From: ynk <evils.ynk@gmail.com>

Fix the IPA QMI handshake with vendor modem firmware:

- Allocate SMEM item 497 (IPA filter table region, 0xb000 on IPA v5.5)
  from the AP at probe time and map it 1:1 into the IPA IOMMU domain.
  The modem does not allocate it itself; without it the modem receives
  a zero per-stats address and asserts when the data path is brought up.
- Report the exact (unaligned) physical address of the item in
  per_stats_smem_info, matching vendor ipa3_qmi_init_modem_send_sync_msg().
- Point hw_filter_stats_info at the IPA SRAM filter/route statistics
  region (IPA_MEM_STATS_FILTER_ROUTE, 0x2cd0 on IPA v5.5) instead of a
  hard-coded offset from an older SoC.
- Send INIT_COMPLETE unconditionally; vendor firmware expects it even
  without a prior indication registration.
- Handle the FILTER_INSTALLED_NOTIF (0x24) request the modem sends after
  installing its filter rules.  The modem asserts with
  "msg_id == QMI_IPA_FILTER_INSTALLED_NOTIF_RESP_V01 failed" and its
  initialization stalls (DOG detects stalled initialization) when the
  AP never responds.

Signed-off-by: ynk <evils.ynk@gmail.com>
